This project includes WebAssembly builds of third-party image codec
libraries. Those components are NOT covered by this project's MIT licence;
they remain under their own licences, listed in THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md.

Principal components (see THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md for the full list):
- MozJPEG (IJG / Mozilla) — used by @dusrel/image-jpeg
- libwebp (Google) — used by @dusrel/image-webp
- libavif and libaom (Alliance for Open Media) — used by @dusrel/image-avif
- Rust PNG crate, OxiPNG, resize / hqx / magic-kernel (Rust ecosystem) —
  used by @dusrel/image-png, @dusrel/image-oxipng, @dusrel/image-resize
- libjxl (JPEG XL team) — used by @dusrel/image-jxl (experimental)
- libimagequant — used by @dusrel/image-quantize

The codec packaging approach is modelled on jSquash and Google Squoosh
(Apache License 2.0). Full attribution is generated from the exact dependency
versions used in each build (see docs/WASM_BUILD.md).
